          "statement": "Input a graph from [[def-finite-straight-line-computational-program]], an admissible point $x$, and a direction $v\\in\\mathbb R^n$. Require every primitive to be $C^1$ on its declared open domain or supplied as a piecewise-$C^1$ primitive with the branch rules of the graph definition. Evaluate all primal node values in topological order and store the tape. Set each input tangent to $\\dot x_i=v_i$. For each operation $j=1,\\ldots,T$, compute\n$$\\dot z_j=D\\phi_j(z_{p_{j,1}},\\ldots,z_{p_{j,r_j}})(\\dot z_{p_{j,1}},\\ldots,\\dot z_{p_{j,r_j}}).$$\nReturn the primal scalar output $f(x)$ and its tangent: return $(z_o,\\dot z_o)$ if $o$ is an operation node, and $(x_i,v_i)$ if $o$ is input coordinate $i$. If the input is outside the admissible domain, return DOMAIN_ERROR; if a piecewise primitive is at a branch boundary or has no unique strict active branch, return NONDIFFERENTIABLE and no tangent. All derivative evaluations in this definition are exact real-arithmetic operations on the specified primitive maps.",
