          "statement": "Input a $C^2$ graph, a point $x$, and direction $v$. Run [[alg-forward-mode-automatic-differentiation]] and retain its primal tape and all input and operation tangents. If that call returns DOMAIN_ERROR or NONDIFFERENTIABLE, return the same status and stop without a Hessian-vector product. Otherwise initialize every operation and input cotangent and tangent-cotangent accumulator to zero. Seed the output by setting its cotangent/tangent-cotangent pair to $(1,0)$: if $o$ is an operation, set $(\\bar z_o,\\dot{\\bar z}_o)=(1,0)$; if $o$ is input coordinate $i$, set $(\\bar x_i,\\dot{\\bar x}_i)=(1,0)$. In reverse topological order, for each node $j$ and parent slot $k$, let $A_{j,k}=D_k\\phi_j(z_{p_{j,1}},\\ldots,z_{p_{j,r_j}})$, compute\n$$c_{j,k}=A_{j,k}^{T}\\bar z_j,\\qquad \\dot c_{j,k}=A_{j,k}^{T}\\dot{\\bar z}_j+\\bigl(DA_{j,k}(z_{p_{j,1}},\\ldots,z_{p_{j,r_j}})[\\dot z_{p_{j,1}},\\ldots,\\dot z_{p_{j,r_j}}]\\bigr)^{T}\\bar z_j,$$\nand add $c_{j,k}$ and $\\dot c_{j,k}$ to the parent's cotangent and tangent-cotangent accumulators. Use $(\\bar x_i,\\dot{\\bar x}_i)$ for input coordinate $i$ and $(\\bar z_\\ell,\\dot{\\bar z}_\\ell)$ for operation node $\\ell$. If the same parent occurs in multiple slots, add every slot contribution.\nReturn $(\\dot{\\bar x}_1,\\ldots,\\dot{\\bar x}_n)$. Repeated parent slots receive separate additions. The admissible case requires every primitive evaluation to be in its declared domain and, for a piecewise primitive, on a unique strict active branch; a branch boundary or ambiguous selection returns NONDIFFERENTIABLE through the initial call. The transpose is the real Euclidean transpose, not a complex adjoint.",
          "strategy": "Input a $C^2$ graph, a point $x$, and direction $v$. Run [[alg-forward-mode-automatic-differentiation]] and retain its primal tape and all input and operation tangents. If that call returns DOMAIN_ERROR or NONDIFFERENTIABLE, return the same status and stop without a Hessian-vector product. Otherwise initialize every operation and input cotangent and tangent-cotangent accumulator to zero. Seed the output by setting its cotangent/tangent-cotangent pair to $(1,0)$: if $o$ is an operation, set $(\\bar z_o,\\dot{\\bar z}_o)=(1,0)$; if $o$ is input coordinate $i$, set $(\\bar x_i,\\dot{\\bar x}_i)=(1,0)$. In reverse topological order, for each node $j$ and parent slot $k$, let $A_{j,k}=D_k\\phi_j(z_{p_{j,1}},\\ldots,z_{p_{j,r_j}})$, compute\n$$c_{j,k}=A_{j,k}^{T}\\bar z_j,\\qquad \\dot c_{j,k}=A_{j,k}^{T}\\dot{\\bar z}_j+\\bigl(DA_{j,k}(z_{p_{j,1}},\\ldots,z_{p_{j,r_j}})[\\dot z_{p_{j,1}},\\ldots,\\dot z_{p_{j,r_j}}]\\bigr)^{T}\\bar z_j,$$\nand add $c_{j,k}$ and $\\dot c_{j,k}$ to the parent's cotangent and tangent-cotangent accumulators. Use $(\\bar x_i,\\dot{\\bar x}_i)$ for input coordinate $i$ and $(\\bar z_\\ell,\\dot{\\bar z}_\\ell)$ for operation node $\\ell$. If the same parent occurs in multiple slots, add every slot contribution.\nReturn $(\\dot{\\bar x}_1,\\ldots,\\dot{\\bar x}_n)$. Repeated parent slots receive separate additions. The admissible case requires every primitive evaluation to be in its declared domain and, for a piecewise primitive, on a unique strict active branch; a branch boundary or ambiguous selection returns NONDIFFERENTIABLE through the initial call. The transpose is the real Euclidean transpose, not a complex adjoint.",
