          "statement": "Let $f$ be the scalar output of a finite $C^2$ graph on a fixed strict branch. At every admissible $x$ and direction $v$, the forward-over-reverse algorithm returns $D(\\operatorname{grad} f)(x)v$, the Hessian-vector product $H_f(x)v$. No Hessian symmetry assumption is needed for this identity.",
