      "scaffold": "research/plan-numerical-optimization-track.md",
      "description": "Controlling repaired prose: research/plan-numerical-optimization-track.md, pair DIF2, and its exact incorporated mathematical-contract appendix. Read the complete repaired contract, preserved scope/amendments/examples, and actual supplier restrictions before authoring. Canonical statistics/linear algebra methods remain at their published homes; only new numerical variants/results and missing typed prerequisites are authored here.\n\n{\"scope\": \"Define a finite straight-line differentiable scalar/vector program, primal tape, forward tangents, reverse cotangents, elementary derivative primitives and Hessian-vector products via nested modes. Prove forward and reverse correctness by topological induction/chain rule; reverse gradient work bounded by a fixed multiple of primal work for the declared bounded-arity primitive set, storage O(tape), excluding opaque solver calls. Prove checkpoint replay invariance and a concrete binomial checkpoint schedule cost/storage bound. Explain branchwise derivatives, nondifferentiable branches and floating-point program versus real-program derivative. Implicit differentiation requires nonsingular Jacobian, proved from the existing implicit function theorem; stopping an iterative solver and differentiating iterations gives a different target with a quantified residual sensitivity. \", \"proof_route\": \"Exact proof design/recurrences and same-owner lemma obligations are embedded in scope and full verbatim contract; source theorem hypotheses must be verified before authoring.\", \"examples\": \"small shared-expression graph; reverse ODE-step tape; implicit linear solve adjoint.\", \"binding_amendments\": [], \"canonical_reuse_rule\": \"Use actual published canonical algorithms/definitions, author only new method variants/results and owned missing typed prerequisites.\", \"prerequisite_ownership\": [{\"owner\": \"DIF2\", \"obligation\": \"DIF2 owns every missing intermediate lemma and proof prerequisite described in