          "statement": "Let $C$ be the row-shift companion matrix for the monic polynomial $\\rho/\\alpha_k$, where $\\rho$ is the characteristic polynomial of a $k$-step method. For a complex vector $v$, set $\\|v\\|_\\infty=\\max_i|v_i|$ and for a matrix $A$ set $\\|A\\|_\\infty=\\max_i\\sum_j|A_{ij}|$. Then\n\n$$\\sup_{n\\ge0}\\|C^n\\|_\\infty<\\infty$$\n\nif and only if $\\rho$ satisfies the root condition from [[def-linear-multistep-method-consistency-order-and-root-condition]]. Consequently the homogeneous recurrence is zero-stable exactly under that root condition.",
